  "dispatch_method": "Untimed instrumented product binary with three integer counters summed at worker destruction. Count split probes reaching the preset lookup, split actions rejected before entering their frame, and nested conjunctive arms rejected before their continuations. Split and nested counts are actual rejected trials, including repeated labels. They exclude ordinary false guards after entry. Same configs, worker counts and affinity. No timings above use the instrumented build.",
  "interpretation": "Flint executes many tests against the same compiled input table and binding. A worker can compare the full persistent table, scalar binding, and field before reusing its selected string. Redundant per-guard memo probes and table allocations disappear. Bakery starts with all reachable states under ISpec; its Init-only control never enters Next. Treat its small total differences as neutral. These controls do not predict a three-barrier wall time.",
  "native_peer_followup": "https://github.com/Chelis-Lang/dive/issues/1302"
}
